 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Points are listed for the global objects (15000 + n), outdoor unit 1 (OU block = (OU x 20) + 10000, OU 1-12) and indoor unit 1 (IU block = IU x 25, IU 1-128). Names keep the printed XX placeholder; footnote digits after names are removed.",
  "The manual has no access column: _C and the all-units command objects are taken as commandable, _S objects as read-only.",
  "With the Dual-Setpoint function enabled, the single setpoint commands are replaced by the three Dualsetpoint objects; the Temperature Setpoint_S then reports accordingly.",
  "AI offsets 16 and 17 are both printed as \"IUXX_Consumption Today Cool_S\" (the other consumption groups end with a Total object); both are listed as printed.",
  "The filename of the manual says in776air although the title is IN776MHI."
 ],
